{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A[Am]las, my love, you [G]do me wrong
To [Am]cast me off dis[E]courteously
For [Am]I have loved you [G]well and long
De[Am]lighting [E]in your [Am]company
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
[C]Greensleeves was [G]all my joy
And [Am]Greensleeves was [E]my delight
[C]Greensleeves was my [G]heart of gold
And [Am]who but my [E]lady [Am]Greensleeves
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
Your [Am]vows you've broken, [G]like my heart
Oh, [Am]why did you so en[E]rapture me?
Now [Am]I remain in a [G]world apart
But [Am]my heart re[E]mains in cap[Am]tivity
{end_of_verse}

{chorus}

